                    \\sum_{i=1}^{q+1}
                    (-1)^i  ((d_{p+1})^{q+1} a) \otimes ((d_0)^p d_{i}b)
                    \\,.
            %p Each sum seperately is now almost the alternating sum expression of an application of the Moore complex coboundary map, except for one missing term in each sum. But the two missing terms are equal and of opposite sign, so we can add them in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
